course: dictionary
lesson: 11289
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: In Mandarin, one spelling can hide several words. Pinyin is the way we write Chinese sounds with the letters we know, and it uses tone marks: the little signs above the letters. The sign tells you which word you mean.
explain: The spelling «wu» can mean five, dance, noon, or not have. Look at the tone mark and the words around it to know which one. «Wǔ» 五 means five, and it is one of the first numbers you learn: yī, èr, sān, sì, wǔ.
explain: In English, you meet wu in names and in the martial art «wushu». The example sentence is «Wu Zetian ruled as emperor in her own name from 690 to 705, the only woman to do so». Here Wu is a family name, not a number, so the words around it tell you what it means.
fact: Pinyin is a way of writing Chinese sounds using the Latin letters.
fact: Tone marks change the meaning of a pinyin word, so «wǔ» and «wú» are different words.
fact: «Wǔ» 五 means five, and it is learnt early when counting from one to five.
fact: «Wu» is a common Chinese family name, as in «Wu Zetian», who ruled as emperor.
fact: Wu Chinese is a group of Chinese varieties spoken around Shanghai, and it is not an English word.
exercise: In Mandarin, 五 is written «wǔ». What number does it mean? | Nine | Ten | *Five | Three
exercise: What does «wú» mean in Mandarin? | Dance | Five | Noon | *Not have, none
exercise: In the sentence «Wu Zetian ruled as emperor in her own name», what is Wu? | A martial art | A number | *A family name | A dance
test: In English, where do you most often meet the word wu? | In the school dictionary of English words | In football commentary | *In names and in the martial art wushu | Every day in counting
test: What is Wu Chinese? | A type of English tea | A famous dance | *A group of Chinese varieties spoken around Shanghai | A kind of lunch
exam: In «wǔfàn», which means lunch, what does wǔ mean? | Five | *Noon | Not have, none | Dance
